{"ts": 1789713097.436812, "kind": "assistant_text", "text": "I submitted short feature 3, short feature 20 and long feature 32 with a predicted out-of-sample Sharpe of 0.05 (sd 0.3), because I found no evidence of real signal in the panel. That combination scored 0.788 in-sample, which does not clear the search-adjusted bar of 1.026.\n\n- **Single features:** the 40 in-sample Sharpes ranged from \u22120.50 to +0.43, with a cross-sectional standard deviation of about 0.22.\n- **Noise benchmark:** 5,000 daily observations is roughly 20 years, so the sampling error on an annualized Sharpe is about 0.22 under pure noise. The observed spread matches that almost exactly, which puts the estimated signal variance at roughly zero.\n- **Combinations:** I tried three, all built from the strongest singles. The other two were short 3 with short 20 (0.670), and short 3 with long 32 and long 14 (0.757). These numbers are what you would expect from picking the best of 40 noisy features, so I shrank the prediction almost to zero.\n\nThe sd of 0.3 allows for out-of-sample sampling error plus a small chance that one of the features is real. I stopped searching after those three combinations, since more mining would have raised the in-sample number and the selection bias without improving the out-of-sample expectation.\n\nSeparately, the Gmail and Google Calendar connectors are not authorized and stay unavailable until you authorize them in your claude.ai connector settings. They were not needed for this task."}
